{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Until it is poured out.</b> From the nifal binyan, and the meaning is that the evil looks toward us, upon the coming of the king of Assyria to the land of Judah, and the meaning is a decree." "<b>And it shall be.</b> Every desert [will be] like the Carmel, and the Carmel will be reckoned as forest like its former companion."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:20.803760991Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}